  "interpretation": [
    "All four worker outputs matched the pinned jpeg-js full-frame differential reference byte-for-byte; the high-entropy fixture reused the same 20 MiB 4:2:0 JPEG SHA-256 as the prior five-sample GDI+ discrepancy.",
    "The high-entropy ROI contains broad GDI+ differences (900/1024 pixels over 8; maximum 70). The neutral-gray/chroma-edge fixture was sampled in separate vertical, horizontal and checkerboard ROIs: 1000/1024, 1008/1024 and 768/1024 points were over 8, with maxima 120, 136 and 147.",
    "The edge-case differences persist after trimming two pixels from each ROI edge: vertical and horizontal interiors each had 784/784 pixels over 8; the checkerboard interior had 588/784. This rules out the outer ROI edge alone as the cause, but the tiled JPEG image still has neighboring chroma transitions.",
    "The high-chroma synthetic edge cases make chroma reconstruction/phase differences a plausible explanation for GDI+ disagreement, while exact worker/jpeg-js agreement reduces concern about raw-chunk transport corruption. This is an inference, not a proof of which decoder is correct.",
    "The GDI+ tolerance of 8 was calibrated only for 4:4:4. Every 4:2:0 record remains FAIL with thresholdCalibratedForSampling=false; none is evidence to accept fidelity.",
    "The ROIs were selected to investigate a previously observed mismatch and do not estimate whole-image error rates. Each case uses one synthetic worker sample; this does not close general JPEG fidelity, memory, T04 acceptance, or any T05 desktop gate.",
    "The runs did not read/write the system clipboard, send input, show a window, install the package, or use user data. Isolated Electron profiles were removed and cleanup was verified."
